{
  "topic": "Regulated teams push — February–March 2027",
  "topic_details": [
    {
      "heading": "Background",
      "content": "The brief is from Sanne Holloran, Field Marketing, to the Campaign team, dated October 19, 2026. Sanne says she listened to sales calls and reviewed Q3 deck notes, and believes marketing is not reflecting what is working in sales conversations with regulated teams. The campaign is intended to address that gap."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Campaign idea and requested claims",
      "content": "The brief says regulated buyers care first about whether they can trust the vendor, and directs the campaign to lead with FedRAMP. It states that slide 5 of the deck says Wickhold is FedRAMP Authorized and that the notes call this a door opener for public sector and anything touching federal money. The requested headline wording is “Wickhold is FedRAMP Authorized.” SOC 2 Type II, renewed January 2026, should appear beside it. Sanne says this is not well known outside sales and is a stronger story than the company has been telling. These are campaign requirements from the brief, not independently verified claims."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Customer story",
      "content": "Feature Vaskell Health as the centerpiece. The brief describes it as the sales team's go-to healthcare story and says the case study is written and in the folder. The requested result is that audit preparation was cut by three weeks with Wickhold Evenburn; put the three-weeks number up front. Include a quote from Temi Okereke-Voss, Director of Security. The quote's actual wording is not included in the brief. The brief says the account is friendly and the story has been used on healthcare calls this quarter; that does not establish customer publication permission."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Audience",
      "content": "Security leaders at healthcare organizations and at companies selling into the public sector. Platform teams may be pulled in later, but this campaign should speak to the security side. The audience is on the security leadership email list and follows Wickhold on LinkedIn more than anywhere else."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Goals and call to action",
      "content": "The campaign goal is demo requests from regulated security teams. Sales would like 25 qualified demo requests by the end of March. The main action is “Book a demo.” The 25-request figure is an internal campaign target."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Product focus",
      "content": "Evenburn is the product focus, with Wickhold Quenchline as supporting detail."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Channel direction and scope",
      "content": "The sender delegates the asset mix and asks for a recommendation, with rationale and sign-off on the plan. The requested channel boundary is owned channels: social posts, blog posts, landing pages, and emails. This should be a focused push, not a large launch."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Campaign timing and review",
      "content": "The campaign goes live Tuesday, February 16, 2027, and runs through March 31, 2027. The brief says the numbers are already in the deck and hopes review will be quick; this is not an approval or confirmation that claims or customer materials are cleared for publication."
    }
  ],
